      <author>ajsea1sy</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/716682</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/716682#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">cd10ea95cd9a8bf8e30869e91016e19e63205a5d</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:49:01 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa5f1e3dfde7.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aa5f26cb33b6.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;The mod is self explanatory, it will make the Master Sword and/or Hylian Shield unbreakable.&lt;br&gt;Is the stupid gods who created the Master Sword making it need an energy recharge when not fighting Malice-infused enemies, just because "So the hero doesn't abuse it's power"? Well we can throw them out of the window!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Prequisites:&lt;/h1&gt;You shouldn't ungroup the "Unbreakable Hero's Equipment" folders you got from unzipping. Just put it in GraphicsPacks. It won't hurt you, but it's for the sake of tidyness. To keep both parts in one folder. They are intended to be that way, and are technically separate mods for convenience. They are also grouped together in Cemu and individually toggleable.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This won't edit the durability of your Master Sword and/or Hylian Shield! It will stay the same. It won't change it to Durability-Up +, won't set the durability to the integer limit. It only freezes it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Since it will only replace the specific files tying to the items, disabling or removing either mod will undo it safely.</description>
